<urn:usf:cli-field-specification:rule-generate-schema:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A collection-valued property is always present in the canonical projection, including an explicit empty array when minimumCardinality is zero. Minimum collection cardinality constrains array entries, not property presence. Generated required sets include every collection field; optional scalar fields remain absent when minimumCardinality is zero and no source value exists. Missing pair, scope, resource or conflict collections must not be confused with an observed empty collection." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-record-specifications> .
<urn:usf:cli-field-specification:rule-generate-schema:1> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive closed JSON Schema object properties and required sets from record-field relationships. Scalar cardinality maximum one maps to a scalar; collection fields map to bounded unique arrays. Record-valued fields reference the canonical schema identity and definition selected by recordSpecification. Sort property names and set-valued constraints deterministically; preserve declared ordered data only when an ordering rule exists. Compare generated schema canonical JSON with checked-in schema; mismatch refuses. No embedded JSON schema literals or parallel TypeScript field roster." <urn:usf:graph:cli-transition-record-specifications> .
